      "summaryMarkdown": "SPIKE-1 holds for candidate A (release-plz 0.3.172), verified from the raw evidence in `artifacts-temp/agentx/gpux-releases/spike/out/` and the scratch clone's reflog, not only SUMMARY.md. Isolation: scratch `origin` and the untagged clone's `origin` are the local `remote.git`; rel.sh/upd.sh unset GITHUB_TOKEN/GH_TOKEN and point the forge at the 127.0.0.1 Gitea mock (release-plz's forge client, the only retrying HTTP client, uses that base URL); the real checkout has no `v*` tag, its origin/main was last fetched before the spike and only state.json is modified. (1) s1-release: one POST /tags `v1.0.0` at the 1.0.0 commit (HEAD), one POST /releases; again-run: 31 'Tag v1.0.0 already exists', no POST. (2)/(3) s2/s3 diffs: exactly Cargo.toml (workspace version + 30 requirements), gpui_mobile's inline `gpux` requirement, 31 own lock version lines 1.0.0->1.0.1 and nothing else, fork `-gpux.1` requirements untouched, one `## [1.0.1]` section, no untracked CHANGELOG; scenario commits touch only crates/gpui_platform resp. crates/gpui_mobile; `version.workspace` count unchanged (33). s3-release tags v1.0.1. (4) feat -> 1.1.0; the import commit (API break stated in body, Migration footer) stays 1.1.0 with every requirement 1.1.0 and the nested Migration line; the plain feat has none (the import commit was tested on top of a plain feat, which still proves it is not treated as breaking). (5) six non-release types touching crates/gpui: 'no commit matches release_commits', no diff. (6) s6/final-s6: one tag at the committed release commit, release body = new section, second run no POST, following update no-op. Final config differs from the run of (1)-(3) only in `git_release_name` and the Migration-line template, both re-proven by final-s4/final-s6. Observations are supported by obs-* outputs (2.0.0 for `!`/BREAKING CHANGE with a release commit, no release for root-manifest/lock/vendor/README-only fixes, untagged tree: initial release at 1.0.0 with no diff, so no pre-1.0.0 commit affects it). Residual risk for s6, not a defect: the GitHub forge path (git/tags + git/refs, release lookup) was not exercised; the mock covered Gitea's API.",
