      "summaryMarkdown": "Source and tests meet VER-1, RPZ-2 and RPZ-3 and RPZ-1's configuration clauses. VER-1: `cargo metadata --no-deps --offline` gives 31 own packages all 1.0.0 and the 8 forks on `30.0.1-gpux.1`/`0.27.1-gpux.1`; the root diff changes exactly the 30 own requirements, `[workspace.package]` and adds `toml = \"0.9\"`; gpui_mobile's inline requirement is 1.0.0; the Cargo.lock diff is 31 own `version` lines plus `regex` and `toml 0.9.8` in gpux-testkit's list (no registry entry changed); nothing under vendor/ changed. RPZ-1: release-plz.toml equals the spike's proven file apart from comments; the tests check [workspace] strictly (exact key count), gpux keys and `changelog_include` against the members, one entry per member with forks `release = false` and others only `version_group`, the release_commits regex on all 12 sample subjects, the skip/group parsers (RayX.CLI's groups plus `^Merge `), header and Migration template. RPZ-2: workflow matches RayX.CLI's except the documented `needs: release` and `version: \"0.3.172\"` (checkout@v7 follows Gpux's ci.yml); tests assert both jobs line-wise, the only secret, no run/cargo/testkit/lane step and that no other workflow has a push trigger (an inline `on:` form fails loudly). RPZ-3: CHANGELOG starts with the configured header; facts verified against zed-imports.tsv (d544470d1d, 2026-10-05; #64718/#64842 on 2026-10-07), README (platform table, fast mode, EditableText, fork notes), docs/testing.md (lanes A-G) and docs/upstream/accesskit-macos-tables-expanded.md; no per-commit history invented. The Distribution paragraph describes s4's declarations and rayx 1.4.0 ahead of s4/s6, which the final review must re-verify. The two spike-proven values (`git_release_name`, nested `  - Migration:` line) are now recorded with reasons in `d-release-tooling-proven` and named in RPZ-1 (finding S2-RPZ1-DESIGN-RECORD resolved; spec-only delta, source unchanged).",
